  "text": "Pet Cancer Support Group | The Oncology Service\nHours & Contact\nTOS - Leesburg\n(571) 209-1176\nleesburg@tosvets.com\nTOS - Richmond\n(804) 999-0001\nrichmond@tosvets.com\nTOS - Springfield\n(703) 451-8900, option 2\nspringfield@tosvets.com\nfacebook\ninstagram\nMenu\nServices\nMedical Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nStereotactic Radiation Therapy\nOutpatient Imaging\nElectrochemotherapy\nAbout Us\nMeet the Team\nVeterinarians\nTOS Leesburg - Veterinarians\nTOS Richmond - Veterinarians\nTOS Springfield - Veterinarians\nSupport Staff\nTOS Leesburg - Support Staff\nTOS Richmond - Support Staff\nTOS Springfield - Support Staff\nYour First Visit\nWhen Your Pet is a Patient\nPayment Options\nClinical Studies\nCareers\nLeesburg\nRichmond\nSpringfield\nTestimonials\nResources\nForms\nLeesburg Forms\nRichmond Forms\nSpringfield Forms\nFAQs\nPet Chemotherapy Guide\nDiscounts\nGrief Resources\nNutrition For The Canine Oncology Patient\nNutrition For The Feline Oncology Patient\nPet Emergency & Urgent Care Resources\nEvents\nPet Loss Support Group\nPet Cancer Support Group\nBlog\nCats\nDogs\nOther\nLocations\nLeesburg\nLeesburg Referral Form\nLeesburg DVM Referring Form\nRichmond\nSpringfield\nRequest an Appointment\nSearch\nButton Bar\nClient Portal\nrVetLink Portal\nReferral Forms\nPet Cancer Support Group\nWe and our friends at\nFETCH a Cure\nunderstand how difficult it can be to receive the news that your pet has cancer. In addition to providing education and funding assistance for pet owners, FETCH a Cure aims to offer support and hope. Our monthly virtual meetings give participants the opportunity to share their experience with others who are pursuing treatment for their pet or have been through the pet cancer journey in the past.\nMeetings are held on the third Thursday of each month via Zoom.\nClick here to register\nand receive the Zoom link for the meeting.\nThis event is not intended to provide medical advice or take the place of information you receive from your pet’s veterinarian.\nThis monthly online event is sponsored by\nThe Oncology Service\nand\nJames River Veterinary Surgery\n.\nFETCH a Cure is a 501 ©(3) non-profit organization focused on improving the quality of life for our pets. Our vision is simple: A community where no one is denied a choice for their pet due to lack of options, education or funding.\nAttendees are encouraged to make a donation to the nonprofit FETCH a Cure. FETCH works to give pets and their owners more quality time together in the face of a cancer diagnosis. To donate, visit:\nhttps://fetchacure.org/donate/annual-fund/\nShare this content\ntwitter\nemail\npinterest\nfacebook\nHow Are We Doing?\nreview us!\nVisit our office to get the latest in top-quality veterinary care along with unparalleled service\nLinks\nAbout Us\nServices\nResources\nContact Us\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nLogin / Account\nGet In Touch\nTOS - Leesburg\n(571) 209-1176\nleesburg@tosvets.com\nTOS - Richmond\n(804) 999-0001\nrichmond@tosvets.com\nTOS - Springfield\n(703) 451-8900, option 2\nspringfield@tosvets.com\nHow Are We Doing?\nReview Us\nfacebook\ninstagram\nX\nThe Oncology Service - Springfield\nThe Oncology Service - Richmond\nThe Oncology Service - Leesburg\n©2025 The Oncology Service. Resource Articles ©2025 KARMAjack. All Rights Reserved.\nVeterinary websites by KARMAjack\nNotice\nTemporary Closure Notice\nOur hospital will be closed from\nSeptember 8–12\nfor unexpected facility repairs.\nWe’re working quickly to get everything resolved. In the meantime, our team will be monitoring our email and voicemail remotely.\nThank you for your patience and understanding, we can’t wait to welcome you and your pets back soon!\nSee other locations\nDismiss",
